<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Pakistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–<a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> was the eastern wing of Pakistan from 1955, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-bengal">East Bengal</a> was renamed, until 1971. Though it held most of Pakistan's population, its people resented political and economic domination by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a>. After the 1970 election and the army's crackdown, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangladesh-liberation-war">Bangladesh Liberation War</a> ended with its independence as Bangladesh in December 1971.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-pakistan.jpg" alt="East Pakistan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mhatopzz · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Pakistan_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
